// Santa's visit, once a winter: the first time the ninja sleeps at home in a
// winter, with no festival on, he comes down the chimney and leaves a present
// on the shelf by the bed (village/SantaVisit, HomeScreen, the chimney in
// HubScreen). Read by com.kagebi.data.VillageCatalog; checked by
// ContentValidator.
//
// "santa" is what the present holds: "gold", "shards" of gem (the lucky
// wheel's tickets), and "stones" socket stones of tier "stoneTier", each of
// a colour picked at random. "keepsake" is the letter in it, kept the first
// time only.
//
// "keepsakes" are things given to be kept rather than used: shown in the bag
// under their own tab, read there, and listed in the dictionary. Each one's
// "icon" is a region of ui.atlas; "source" names where it comes from,
// codex.from.<source>. Its words are keepsake.<id>.name and .desc, and the
// letter itself keepsake.<id>.text.1, .text.2 on, a paragraph each.
{
  "santa": {"gold": 1000, "shards": 5, "stoneTier": 2, "stones": 1, "keepsake": "santa_letter"},

  "keepsakes": [
    {"id": "santa_letter", "icon": "ui/paper/scroll5", "source": "christmas"}
  ]
}
